  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to the Multisectoral National Strategic Plan for TB Control 2016-2020 (PENMTB) in El Salvador - El Salvador (01-Jan-2016-31-Dec-2018)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">El Salvador, Tuberculosis, Ministry of Health of the Republic of El Salvador (MOH)This program has the following goals: Detect TB promptly, reduce mortality and start the process of Advanced TB Control and Pre-elimination as a public health issue in selected municipalities, applying WHO&#x2019;s post-2015 strategy nationally, with multisectoral support and involvement, particularly the support of civil society organizations. The objectives of this program are: Detect at least 90&#xa0;percent of bacteriologically confirmed cases of drug-resistant TB (RR-TB and/or MDR-TB) notified to the national TB program.  Detect at least 90&#xa0;percent of respiratory symptoms and cases of TB, prioritizing the municipalities with the largest detection gaps.  Promptly diagnose and treat TB in at-risk groups (PDL, diabetics or immunosuppressed patients, contacts, health workers, children).  Promptly diagnose and treat TB/HIV coinfection.  Strengthen the health system.  Successfully treat more than 90% percent of cases detected.  Treat 100&#xa0;percent of bacteriologically confirmed cases of drug-resistant TB (RR-TB and/or MDR-TB) notified to the national TB program</narrative>
  </description>
